oot cause of the order displaying two prices\\nRoot cause of the temporarily missing color-coded shipping bar in the admin panel\\nWhether rebuild kits should be offered as customizable bundle products (Kelly to consider)\"',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'openrouter','~anthropic/claude-fable-latest',NULL,'2026-07-21 21:08:39',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-21 21:08:39','2026-07-21 21:08:39'),(2,101,'Transpart- Weekly Meeting\n\nJul 21, 2026\n\nJean Paul Hanna kelly.a.hufford@gmail.com Nour Ayman Donia Attwa\n\nStrategic growth plans and technical improvements regarding platform integrations and system security updates were reviewed and finalized.\n\nInternational Business Development\nInternational B2B supplier model proposed for parts distribution to American car owners.\nTargeted marketing campaigns planned to evaluate viability of international regions.\n\nAutomated Marketing and Support\nChatbot flow analysis underway to improve automated response rates and information quality.\nClavio implementation planned to enable segmented automated marketing emails based on customer events.\nShipping policy communication refinement anticipated to prevent customer dissatisfaction regarding delivery speeds.\n\nSystem Administration and Maintenance\nBundled product functionality deployed to production to improve order clarity in admin and storefront views.\nFuture component customization for rebuild kits proposed to allow specific item removal.\nAdministrative UI color-coded shipping alerts verified as functional following server maintenance.\nMandatory security hotfix deployment scheduled for this week or early next week.\n\nNext steps\n[Nour Ayman] Analyze Chat Logs: Perform a deep analysis of chat logs to identify automated versus manual responses. Improve the flow and information based on the findings.\n[Jean Paul Hanna] Connect Clavio: Establish a connection with Clavio for automated marketing emails based on customer event segments.\n[Jean Paul Hanna] Integrate Ship Station: Connect the Ship