Ayman: Bye.\nIrem Aydin: Bye-bye.\nDonia Attwa: bye.\n\n\nTranscription ended after 01:04:51\n\nThis editable transcript was computer generated and might contain errors. People can also change the text after it was created.\n','Technopath and Cambro met to review the cookie consent banner and progress on the CRO/development task list. JP demoed a new cookie consent banner deployed to production (bottom-of-screen placement, \'Allow all\' button on the right). Concerns were raised about the red button color and whether translation into German and Italian is needed; Cambro will ask their Midsummer team for feedback and clarify translation requirements. The team agreed to improve the shared tracking sheet (adding ticket numbers, request dates, estimated times, and brief detail notes) and to work through the task list during future sessions. Priorities were set to focus on high and highest items first, given ongoing overachievement of scope. Several tasks are ready for deployment and scheduled to go to production on Friday, with staging deadlines around Tuesday, August 11. Discussion also covered the product FAQ feature (an underlying extension bug must be fixed before applying the vertical FAQ design), color/size swatch work (split between Cambro data-entry tasks and Technopath code tasks), a product enablement issue (products not enabled across all store views), and how to bulk-update product statuses via Firebear import/export. A tutorial/recording session on Firebear was scheduled for Monday at 9:00. Irem was set up with staging credentials to run tests.','Meeting Summary and Next Steps – Cambro','<p>Hi Irem,</p><p>Thank you for taking the time to meet with us on Wednesday, August 5, 2026. Here\'s a summary of our discussion and agreed next steps:</p><h3>Key Points Discussed</h3><ul><li>We deployed a new cookie consent banner to production. It now appears at the bottom of the screen (instead of a center pop-up) with the \"Allow all\" button on the right. You can review it live and provide feedback.</li><li>The banner currently uses red styling to match Cambro branding; there was a suggestion to consider blue instead. We recommend gathering feedback from the Midsummer team on the design and color.</li><li>Cookiebot supports adding languages (e.g., German and Italian). Translations are not automatic and would need to be provided. Please confirm your translation requirements, noting that German (not Dutch) is the required language.</li><li>We reviewed the shared CRO/development tracking sheet and agreed to enhance it with ticket numbers, request dates, estimated times, and brief detail notes for clarity.</li><li>We agreed to prioritize high and highest priority items first, then move to medium/low items later.</li><li>Product FAQ: An existing FAQ extension on staging is not currently working. This bug must be fixed before we can implement the approved vertical FAQ design.</li><li>Color and size swatches: Some items (duplicate colors, multicolor icon) are data-entry tasks on Cambro\'s side; others (missing text labels, borders) are code tasks on our side. We will apply the same approach to capacity/size swatches.</li><li>Product enablement: We reviewed how to bulk-update product statuses across store views using a Firebear export/import. We will provide guidance and staging access so you can test.</li><li>Stock sync (AS400 &lt;-&gt; Magento): This runs on the Cambro IT side via the Magento API; we have no direct visibility. We recommend confirming with Mike and the team that stock is updating.</li></ul><h3>Decisions Made</h3><ul><li>The new cookie consent banner will remain live for now (old version can be restored if needed).</li><li>Team will focus on high and highest priority items before medium/low items.</li><li>Deployments to production will be batched and done once per week (end of week / Friday).</li><li>The FAQ extension bug must be resolved before implementing the vertical FAQ design.</li><li>Asana links (rather than new help desk tickets) will be added to the sheet for Asana-based tasks.</li><li>A Firebear tutorial/recording session will be held Monday at 9:00.</li></ul><h3>Action Items</h3><ul><li><strong>Review new cookie consent banner and share feedback</strong> – Irem (Cambro) – Aug 7, 2026</li><li><strong>Ask Midsummer team for feedback on banner design/color</strong> – Irem (Cambro) – Aug 7, 2026</li><li><strong>Confirm translation requirements (German, Italian) for consent banner</strong> – Irem (Cambro) – Aug 7, 2026</li><li><strong>Update tracking sheet with ticket numbers, dates, estimates, and detail notes</strong> – Nour (Technopath) – Aug 11, 2026</li><li><strong>Deliver configurable products (cheapest selection) task to staging</strong> – Nour (Technopath) – Aug 11, 2026</li><li><strong>Fix FAQ extension bug on staging</strong> – Nour (Technopath) – Aug 11, 2026</li><li><strong>Deploy ready items to production and test</strong> – Nour (Technopath) – Aug 7, 2026</li><li><strong>Investigate why new-products flag / product enablement is inconsistent</strong> – Donia (Technopath) – (TBD)</li><li><strong>Provide color swatch details and confirm impact of switching swatches</strong> – Donia (Technopath) – (TBD)</li><li><strong>Send capacity/size swatch details for ticket 2186</strong> – Irem (Cambro) – (TBD)</li><li><strong>Test product status bulk-update via Firebear on staging</strong> – Irem (Cambro) – (TBD)</li><li><strong>Review Figma designs (category and product page) and provide feedback</strong> – JP (Technopath) – (TBD)</li></ul><h3>Open Questions</h3><ul><li>Should the \"Allow all\" button be red or blue? (Awaiting Midsummer feedback)</li><li>Does the consent banner need to be translated, and who will provide/approve the legal translations?</li><li>Is the AS400 &lt;-&gt; Magento stock sync updating correctly? (To be confirmed with Cambro IT / Mike)</li><li>Will switching color/size swatches affect the code-side tasks, or should the team focus on capacity swatche