t grid. Let\'s talk about it.\nJean Paul Hanna: Yeah.\nNour Ayman: Okay, great. And uh and I think that\'s it from last week.\nKelly Hufford: Okay.\nNour Ayman: Uh do you have anything else you want us to work on beside these two new\nKelly Hufford: Nope.\nNour Ayman: tickets?\nKelly Hufford: Nope. That\'s all.\nNour Ayman: Okay.\nJean Paul Hanna: Okay, Kelly,\nKelly Hufford: Okay.\nJean Paul Hanna: good to see you.\nKelly Hufford: Good to see you, too. Thanks. See you.\nJean Paul Hanna: See you.\nDonia Attwa: Thank you.\nNour Ayman: Bye.\nKelly Hufford: Bye.\nJean Paul Hanna: Bye.\nKelly Hufford: Bye. Thanks Donia.\nDonia Attwa: Thank you. Bye.\n\n\nTranscription ended after 00:14:49\n\nThis editable transcript was computer generated and might contain errors. People can also change the text after it was created.','The Transpart weekly meeting covered operational and technical updates. On inventory, Nour shared a list of Recon torque converter products; Kelly confirmed core charges apply only to specific SKUs and will review the list against Transcend\'s core charge data and return it. The team agreed core charges will be applied manually per product. For international logistics, a new UPS carrier account designated for international orders has been added in ShipStation; Donia will connect it and disconnect the previous international carrier. On technical issues, the bonded products kit is failing to deploy in the new cluster (though it works in staging) and the team is actively fixing it. OTP verification emails for order status checks are landing in spam, causing customers to abandon verification; Nour raised a ticket with eDesk, and the team agreed to use Klaviyo (already integrated) as an alternative if eDesk cannot resolve it. Kelly reported chatbot errors including irrelevant links sent to a satisfied customer and failure to answer shipping speed questions (e.g., UPS Next Day Air / Second Day Air). The team agreed to document problematic conversations with correct-response guidance to train the chatbot, and JP and Donia will design a training interface (possibly in Retool, or a sheet-based hybrid — final format to be determined). Kelly confirmed product fitment data is available in Retool from Transcend, and noted part numbers are being continuously updated to align with that data. JP will extract fitment information from the Retool and Transcend databases.','Meeting Summary and Next Steps – Transpart','<p>Hi Kelly,</p><p>Thank you for taking the time to meet with us on Wednesday, August 5, 2026. Here\'s a summary of our discussion and agreed next steps:</p><h3>Key Points Discussed</h3><ul><li><strong>Recon Core Charges:</strong> Core charges apply only to specific SKUs within the Recon torque converter list. You\'ll review the list against the core charge data from Transcend and send back the updated document.</li><li><strong>International Shipping (ShipStation):</strong> A new UPS account designated for international orders has been set up. We will connect it in ShipStation and disconnect the previous international carrier.</li><li><strong>Bonded Products Kit:</strong> We identified a deployment issue in the new cluster (the kit works correctly in staging) and are actively working on the fix.</li><li><strong>Order Status OTP Emails:</strong> Verification emails are landing in spam, preventing some customers from completing order status checks. We\'ve raised a ticket with eDesk and will move OTP sending to Klaviyo if the issue isn\'t resolved on their side.</li><li><strong>Chatbot Improvements:</strong> Thank you for flagging the incorrect responses (irrelevant kit links and missing shipping-speed answers). These examples will be used as training data, and we\'ll build a structured process to log errors and define correct response instructions, including when the bot should escalate to a support ticket.</li><li><strong>Product Data:</strong> Fitment information is available in Retool from Transcend, and your ongoing part number updates will continue to improve data matching.</li></ul><h3>Decisions Made</h3><ul><li>Core charges will be applied manually on a per-product basis for the relevant SKUs.</li><li>The new UPS account will be connected for international shipments only, and the previous international carrier will be disconnected.</li><li>Klaviyo will be used for OTP notifications if the eDesk ticket does not resolve the spam deliverability issue.</li><li>A tracking process will be created to log chatbot errors and establish standardized response instructions for training.</li></ul><h3>Action Items</h3><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><th>Action Item</th><th>Owner</th><th>Due Date</th></tr><tr><td>Review the Recon torque converter list, apply relevant core charges, and return the updated document</td><td>Kelly Hufford</td><td>Aug 6, 2026 (today/tomorrow as discussed)</td></tr><tr><td>Review the manual process for adding core charges to products and report findings</td><td>Nour Ayman</td><td>TBD</td></tr><tr><td>Connect the new UPS carrier for international orders and disconnect the previous carrier</td><td>Donia Attwa</td><td>TBD</td></tr><tr><td>Extract product fitment information from the Retool and Transcend databases</td><td>Jean Paul Hanna</td><td>TBD</td></tr><tr><td>Design an interface to streamline chatbot training and response management</td><td>Jean Paul Hanna & Donia Attwa</td><td>TBD</td></tr></table><h3>Open Questions</h3><ul><li>Which specific SKUs from the Recon list require core charges (pending your review).</li><li>Final format for the chatbot training interface (Retool-based, spreadsheet, or a hybrid) — to be evaluated before implementation.</li><li>Whether eDesk can resolve the OTP spam deliverability issue, or if we proceed with the Klaviyo transition.</li></ul><h3>Next Steps / Next Meeting</h3><p>We\'ll continue with the action items above and reconnect at our next weekly meeting to review progress, including the core charges document, the UPS carrier switch, and chatbot training updates.</p><p>Please don\'t hesitate to reach out if anything needs clarification.</p><p>Best,<br>The Technopath Team</p>','Meeting Summary and Next Steps – Transpart','<p>Hi Kelly,</p><p>Thank you for taking the time to meet with us on Wednesday, August 5, 2026. Here\'s a summary of our discussion and agreed next steps:</p><h3>Key Points Discussed</h3><ul><li><strong>Recon Core Charges:</strong> Core charges apply only to specific SKUs within the Recon torque converter list. You\'ll review the list against the core charge data from Transcend and send back the updated document.</li><li><strong>International Shipping (ShipStation):</strong> A new UPS account designated for international orders has been set up. We will connect it in ShipStation and disconnect the previous international carrier.</li><li><strong>Bonded Products Kit:</strong> We identified a deployment issue in the new cluster (the kit works correctly in staging) and are actively working on the fix.</li><li><strong>Order Status OTP Emails:</strong> Verification emails are landing in spam, preventing some customers from completing order status checks. We\'ve raised a ticket with eDesk and will move OTP sending to Klaviyo if the issue isn\'t resolved on their side.</li><li><strong>Chatbot Improvements:</strong> Thank you for flagging the incorrect responses (irrelevant kit links and missing shipping-speed answers). These examples will be used as training data, and we\'ll build a structured process to log errors and define correct response instructions, including when the bot should escalate to a support ticket.</li><li><strong>Product Data:</strong> Fitment information is available in Retool from Transcend, and your ongoing part number updates will continue to improve data matching.</li></ul><h3>Decisions Made</h3><ul><li>Core charges will be applied manually on a per-product basis for the relevant SKUs.</li><li>The new UPS account will be connected for international shipments only, and the previous international carrier will be disconnected.</li><li>Klaviyo will be used for OTP notifications if the eDesk ticket does not resolve the spam deliverability issue.</li><li>A tracking process will be created to log chatbot errors and establish standardized response instructions for training.</li></ul><h3>Action Items</h3><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tbody><tr><th>Action Item</th><th>Owner</th><th>Due Date</th></tr><tr><td>Review the Recon torque converter list, apply relevant core charges, and return the updated document</td><td>Kelly Hufford</td><td>Aug 6, 2026 (today/tomorrow as discussed)</td></tr><tr><td>Review the manual process for adding core charges to products and report findings</td><td>Nour Ayman</td><td>TBD</td></tr><tr><td>Connect the new UPS carrier for international orders and disconnect the previous carrier</td><td>Donia Attwa</td><td>TBD</td></tr><tr><td>Extract product fitment information from the Retool and Transcend databases</td><td>Jean Paul Hanna</td><td>TBD</td></tr><tr><td>Design an interface to streamline chatbot training and response management</td><td>Jean Paul Hanna &amp; Donia Attwa</td><td>TBD</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Open Questions</h3><ul><li>Which specific SKUs from the Recon list require core charges (pending your review).</li><li>Final format for the chatbot training interface (Retool-based, spreadsheet, or a hybrid) — to be evaluated before implementation.</li><li>Whether eDesk can resolve the OTP spam deliverability issue, or if we proceed with the Klaviyo transition.</li></ul><h3>Next Steps / Next Meeting</h3><p>We\'ll continue with the action items above and reconnect at our next weekly meeting to review progress, including the core charges document, the UPS carrier switch, and chatbot training updates.</p><p>Please don\'t hesitate to reach out if anything needs clarification.</p><p>Best,<br>Nour</p>','[{\"title\": \"Review the Recon torque converter list, apply relevant core charges to applicable SKUs, and return the updated document\", \"due_date\": \"2026-08-06\", \"owner_name\": \"Kelly Hufford\", \"is_customer_facing\": true}, {\"title\": \"Review the manual process for adding core charges to products in the system and report findings\", \"due_date\": null, \"owner_name\": \"Nour Ayman\", \"is_customer_facing\": false}, {\"title\": \"Connect the new UPS carrier account in ShipStation for international orders and disconnect the previous international carrier\", \"due_date\": null, \"owner_name\": \"Donia Attwa\", \"is_customer_facing\": true}, {\"title\": \"Extract product fitment information from the Retool and Transcend databases\", \"due_date\": null, \"owner_name\": \"Jean Paul Hanna\", \"is_customer_facing\": false}, {\"title\": \"Design and evaluate an interface (Retool and/or sheet-based) to streamline chatbot training and response management\", \"due_date\": null, \"owner_name\": \"Jean Paul Hanna\", \"is_customer_facing\": false}, {\"title\": \"Collaborate on the chatbot training interface design and data input workflow\", \"due_date\": null, \"owner_name\": \"Donia Attwa\", \"is_customer_facing\": false}, {\"title\": \"Follow up on the eDesk ticket regarding OTP emails going to spam; if unresolved, proceed with Klaviyo integration for OTP sending\", \"due_date\": null, \"owner_name\": \"Nour Ayman\", \"is_customer_facing\": false}, {\"title\": \"Fix the bonded products kit deployment failure in the new cluster\", \"due_date\": null, \"owner_name\": \"Nour Ayman\", \"is_customer_facing\": false}]','\"Core charges will be applied manually on a per-product basis for the relevant Recon torque converter SKUs.\\nThe new UPS carrier account will be connected in ShipStation for international orders only, and the previous international carrier will be disconnected.\\nKlaviyo will be used for sending OTP verification emails if the eDesk support ticket does not resolve the spam deliverability issue.\\nThe team will create a tracking process (external sheet with comments/instructions) to log chatbot errors and establish standardized response protocols, including escalation-to-ticket rules.\\nJP and Donia will develop an interface to streamline chatbot training data input.\"','\"Which specific SKUs from the Recon torque converter list require core charges (pending Kelly\'s review against Transcend\'s core charge data).\\nFinal format of the chatbot training interface — Retool-built, spreadsheet-based, or a hybrid — still needs to be evaluated (JP and Donia to discuss).\\nWhether eDesk can fix the OTP-to-spam issue on their side, or whether the team proceeds with migrating OTP sending to Klaviyo.\\nRoot cause resolution timeline for the bonded products kit deployment failure in the new cluster (fix in progress, no due date discussed).\\nExact manual process in the system for applying core charges per product (Nour to check and report back).\"',NULL,'2026-08-05 20:56:24','kelly.a.hufford@gmail.com','[\"jp@technopath.co\", \"donia@technopath.co\"]','openrouter','~anthropic/claude-fable-latest',NULL,'2026-08-05 20:55:30',NULL,NULL,'2026-08-05 20:54:48','2026-08-05 20:56:24');
