INSERT INTO `meeting_preps` VALUES (1,11,'TRAN','project = TRAN AND updated >= \'2026-07-07\' ORDER BY updated DESC','PROJECT: Transpart – Weekly Meeting (Wed, July 15, 2026, 4:30 PM)\nAttendees: JP, Nour, Donia (internal); Kelly Hufford (external)\nClient/Industry/Platform per CRM: [Information Not Available] — Jira data indicates an Adobe Commerce / Magento 2.4.7-p7 store on Nexcess hosting.\n\n=== OVERALL HEALTH ===\nModerately healthy. Good delivery velocity (6 items completed, including 2 Highest-priority items), 7 items actively in progress or ready for dev, and 2 items ready for deployment. RISK AREA: a large backlog of 23 blocked/on-hold items, including 1 Highest-priority and 1 High-priority item sitting in backlog, plus an unpatched security CVE still in \'Ready For Dev\'.\n\n=== COMPLETED SINCE LAST MEETING (6) ===\n- TRAN-1289: Reconciled out-of-stock flag with storefront behavior (Nour)\n- TRAN-1108: Code review and deployment (Mostafa)\n- TRAN-1107: Fixed \'Login as Customer\' redirect bug on production (Mostafa)\n- TRAN-1284: AI Chatbot deployed to production, optimization initialized (Nour) — HIGHEST priority, key win\n- TRAN-1285: Dry run test (Nour)\n- TRAN-1263: \'Add to Cart\' button added to Featured Products (Nour) — HIGHEST priority\n\n=== IN PROGRESS / READY FOR DEV (7) ===\n- TRAN-268: Project Management (Nour) — ongoing\n- TRAN-1281: Bundle & Configurable Products catalog update (JP) — In Progress\n- TRAN-1292: Merge eDesk accounts to support@tecnopath (Nour) — Ready For Dev\n- TRAN-1291: Verify ShipStation & Klaviyo connections (Nour) — Ready For Dev\n- TRAN-1290: Analyze chatbot conversations with AI (Nour) — Ready For Dev, follows chatbot launch\n- TRAN-1286: SECURITY hotfix CVE-2025-54236 (SessionReaper) on Adobe Commerce 2.4.7-p7 (Mostafa) — Ready For Dev. Recommend prioritizing; security exposure until patched.\n- TRAN-1255: Product Kits import job failing at 90% (Mostafa) — Ready For Dev\n\n=== READY FOR DEPLOYMENT (2) ===\n- TRAN-1275: Estimated Shipping Rules & Hold Status email notifications (Mostafa)\n- TRAN-1283: Simplified purchase flow/display for Rebuild Kits & Packages (Mostafa)\nBoth are candidates for customer sign-off before deploying.\n\n=== BLOCKERS & RISKS (23 backlog/on-hold) ===\nKey concerns:\n- TRAN-653 (HIGHEST): Order grid row coloring for UPS shipping (MageWorx) not working — highest priority yet still in backlog with Leo Ho. Needs prioritization decision.\n- TRAN-491 (HIGH): Email notifications for customer group changes — backlog.\n- TRAN-1027: Explicitly blocked by Nexcess (staging \'True Orders\' / no-index issue) — external dependency.\n- TRAN-1071: Klaviyo 6-month campaign calendar — On Hold (Mahmoud). Confirm reason for hold.\n- Stability items in backlog: TRAN-641 (504 gateway timeouts), TRAN-1119 (New Relic response-time spikes), TRAN-1131 (UptimeRobot downtime review) — recurring performance/uptime concerns not being actively worked.\n- 4 unassigned tickets (TRAN-697, TRAN-674, TRAN-868, TRAN-701) — need owners.\n- Data/catalog work stream (TRAN-339, TRAN-530, TRAN-781, TRAN-437) parked in backlog — may relate to JP\'s active bundle/configurable work; check for dependencies.\n\n=== ITEMS NEEDING CUSTOMER INPUT ===\nNo tickets are formally flagged as needing customer input in Jira. However, recommend raising:\n1. Approval/timing for the two Ready-for-Deployment items (shipping rules emails; rebuild kit purchase flow).\n2. Prioritization of the large backlog, especially TRAN-653 (Highest) and TRAN-491 (High).\n3. Klaviyo campaign calendar (TRAN-1071) — confirm whether hold is customer-driven.\n4. Marketing items awaiting direction (TRAN-935, TRAN-821 promo campaigns).\n\n=== KEY TALKING POINTS ===\n1. Celebrate the AI Chatbot production launch; share plan for conversation analysis and optimization (TRAN-1290).\n2. Get deployment window approval for the two ready items.\n3. Flag the security hotfix internally — schedule ASAP, communicate to client at a high level (\'routine security maintenance\').\n4. Discuss backlog grooming: 23 items parked, some high priority — propose a prioritization session.\n5. Confirm status of ShipStation/Klaviyo integration checks before dependent work proceeds.\n6. Note discrepancy: meeting date is July 15 but snapshot and several \'completed\' items are dated after that (up to July 21). Verify meeting date/recurrence before sending the email.','Status Update Before Our Meeting – Unknown Client','<p>Hi Kelly,</p><p>Ahead of our meeting on Wednesday, July 15, 2026, here\'s a quick summary of where things stand:</p><p><strong>Completed Since Last Meeting</strong></p><ul><li>The AI Chatbot is now live on your production site, and we\'ve begun the initial optimization phase.</li><li>An \"Add to Cart\" button has been added to the Featured Products section, making it easier for customers to buy directly from the homepage.</li><li>Fixed an issue where logging in as a customer from the admin was redirecting to the login page instead of starting a session.</li><li>Resolved a discrepancy between the out-of-stock flag and how products actually displayed on the storefront.</li><li>Completed a round of code review, testing, and deployment to keep everything stable.</li></ul><p><strong>Currently In Progress</strong></p><ul><li>Catalog enhancements to support bundled and configurable product options.</li><li>Analysis of chatbot conversations to fine-tune responses and improve the customer experience.</li><li>Verifying the connections with ShipStation and Klaviyo to ensure smooth shipping and email marketing operations.</li><li>Resolving an issue with the product kits import process.</li><li>Consolidating our support inbox setup so all customer inquiries flow through a single support address.</li><li>A routine security update for your store platform.</li></ul><p><strong>Blockers / Items Needing Your Input</strong></p><ul><li>Two enhancements are complete and ready to deploy — the estimated shipping rules with hold-status email notifications, and the simplified purchase flow for Rebuild Kits and Packages. We\'d like your go-ahead and preferred timing for these releases.</li><li>We have a number of items in the backlog, including some higher-priority ones (such as the order grid color coding for UPS shipping methods and email notifications for customer group changes). We\'d like to review priorities with you to make sure we\'re focused on what matters most to your business.</li><li>The Klaviyo 6-month campaign calendar is currently on hold — we\'d like to confirm next steps with you.</li></ul><p><strong>Items Ready for Review</strong></p><ul><li>Estimated shipping rules and hold-status email notifications — ready for your review before deployment.</li><li>Simplified purchase flow and display for Rebuild Kits / Packages — ready for your review before deployment.</li></ul><p><strong>Proposed Agenda</strong></p><ol><li>Recap of completed work, including the AI Chatbot launch</li><li>Review and approval of the two items ready for deployment</li><li>Update on in-progress work (catalog updates, integrations, chatbot optimization)</li><li>Backlog prioritization — aligning on what to tackle next</li><li>Marketing initiatives and Klaviyo campaign planning</li><li>Open questions and next steps</li></ol><p>Please let us know if you\'d like to add anything to the agenda. Looking forward to speaking with you.</p><p>Best,</p>',NULL,NULL,'\"1. Wins & Completed Work Recap (5 min) — AI Chatbot production launch, Featured Products \'Add to Cart\', login-as-customer fix, out-of-stock reconciliation.\\n2. Deployment Approvals (5–10 min) — Review and get sign-off on the two ready-for-deployment items: estimated shipping rules / hold-status email notifications and the simplified Rebuild Kits purchase flow; agree on a deployment window.\\n3. In-Progress Work Update (10 min) — Bundle & configurable products catalog update, chatbot conversation analysis, ShipStation/Klaviyo connection verification, product kits import fix, and the platform security update.\\n4. Backlog Prioritization (10–15 min) — Align on next priorities, with focus on the UPS order grid color coding (Highest), customer group change email notifications (High), and site performance/uptime investigations; assign owners to unassigned items.\\n5. Marketing & Klaviyo (5–10 min) — Status of the on-hold 6-month campaign calendar and pending promo campaigns (Rebuild Kit landing page, promo emails); confirm next steps and dependencies.\\n6. Open Items & Next Steps (5 min) — Customer questions, action items, and confirmation of next meeting.\"','{\"other\": [{\"key\": \"TRAN-1275\", \"status\": \"Ready for Deployment\", \"summary\": \"Configure Estimated Shipping Rules & Hold Status Email Notifications\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-21T16:32:52.211-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Mostafa Naguib\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}, {\"key\": \"TRAN-1283\", \"status\": \"Ready for Deployment\", \"summary\": \"Simplify Purchase Flow & Display for Rebuild Kits / Packages\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-21T05:13:23.896-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Mostafa Naguib\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}], \"in_progress\": [{\"key\": \"TRAN-268\", \"status\": \"In Progress\", \"summary\": \"Project Management \", \"updated\": \"2026-07-21T16:53:11.190-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Nour eldin ayman\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}, {\"key\": \"TRAN-1292\", \"status\": \"Ready For Dev\", \"summary\": \"Merge eDesk accounts of Nour and JP to use support@tecnopath\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-21T16:32:53.085-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Nour eldin ayman\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}, {\"key\": \"TRAN-1291\", \"status\": \"Ready For Dev\", \"summary\": \"Check connection with ShipStation and Klaviyo\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-21T16:32:52.906-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Nour eldin ayman\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}, {\"key\": \"TRAN-1290\", \"status\": \"Ready For Dev\", \"summary\": \"Analyze chatbot conversation with AI\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-21T16:32:52.751-0400\", \"assignee