Standard & Transfer Case Sections\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-21T16:32:51.519-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Nour eldin ayman\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}, {\"key\": \"TRAN-821\", \"status\": \"BACKLOG\", \"summary\": \"Create email campaign to promote the new Rebuild Kit landing page with a 10% discount offer\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-21T16:32:51.516-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Jean Paul Hanna\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}, {\"key\": \"TRAN-1151\", \"status\": \"BACKLOG\", \"summary\": \"Server Error on PDP Banner Image Upload\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-21T16:32:51.175-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Mostafa Naguib\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}, {\"key\": \"TRAN-701\", \"status\": \"BACKLOG\", \"summary\": \"Improve Klaviyo Event Tracking in Magento (Custom Integration)\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-21T16:32:51.174-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Unassigned\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}], \"needs_customer_input\": [], \"completed_since_last_meeting\": [{\"key\": \"TRAN-1289\", \"status\": \"Done\", \"summary\": \"Reconcile out-of-stock flag with actual storefront behavior\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-19T04:50:01.990-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Nour eldin ayman\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}, {\"key\": \"TRAN-1108\", \"status\": \"Done\", \"summary\": \"Code Review and Deployment\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-18T06:54:38.389-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Mostafa Naguib\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}, {\"key\": \"TRAN-1107\", \"status\": \"Done\", \"summary\": \"Login as Customer Redirects to Login Page Instead of Frontend Session (Production Only)\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-18T06:54:14.147-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Mostafa Naguib\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}, {\"key\": \"TRAN-1284\", \"status\": \"Done\", \"summary\": \"Deploy AI Chatbot to Production and Initialize Optimization\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-17T09:46:46.061-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Nour eldin ayman\", \"priority\": \"Highest\"}, {\"key\": \"TRAN-1285\", \"status\": \"Done\", \"summary\": \"Dry run test\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-17T07:44:12.713-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Nour eldin ayman\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}]}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'openrouter','~anthropic/claude-fable-latest',NULL,'2026-07-21 21:07:13',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-21 21:07:13','2026-07-21 21:07:13'),(5,101,'TRAN','project = TRAN AND updated >= \'2026-07-14\' ORDER BY updated DESC','PROJECT HEALTH: Overall AMBER/GREEN. Good delivery velocity this week (5 items completed, including the highest-priority AI Chatbot production deployment), but a large backlog (23 items in blocked/backlog/on-hold) with several aging issues and a pending security hotfix that needs prioritization.\n\nCOMPLETED SINCE LAST MEETING (5):\n- TRAN-1284 (Highest): AI Chatbot deployed to production, optimization initialized — key win, lead with this.\n- TRAN-1289: Out-of-stock flag reconciled with storefront behavior (Nour).\n- TRAN-1107 / TRAN-1108: \'Login as Customer\' production redirect bug fixed, code reviewed and deployed (Mostafa).\n- TRAN-1285: Dry run test completed (Nour).\n\nIN PROGRESS / READY FOR DEV (7):\n- TRAN-1281: Magento Catalog Update — Bundle & Configurable Products (JP, In Progress).\n- TRAN-268: Ongoing Project Management (Nour).\n- TRAN-1286: SECURITY — CVE-2025-54236 (SessionReaper) hotfix for Adobe Commerce 2.4.7-p7 is only \'Ready For Dev\'. Recommend escalating priority; security patches should not sit in queue.\n- TRAN-1290: Analyze chatbot conversations with AI (follow-on from chatbot launch).\n- TRAN-1291: Verify ShipStation & Klaviyo connections.\n- TRAN-1292: Merge eDesk accounts (Nour/JP) to support@tecnopath — internal housekeeping.\n- TRAN-1255: Product Kits import job failing at 90% (Mostafa) — could impact catalog work.\n\nREADY FOR DEPLOYMENT (2):\n- TRAN-1275: Estimated Shipping Rules & Hold Status Email Notifications.\n- TRAN-1283: Simplified Purchase Flow & Display for Rebuild Kits/Packages.\nBoth should be scheduled for deployment — confirm deployment window with client if needed.\n\nBLOCKERS & RISKS (23 items in backlog/on hold — notable ones):\n- TRAN-653 (HIGHEST priority, still BACKLOG): Order Grid Row Coloring for UPS Shipping Methods (MageWorx) — highest priority item sitting in backlog is a red flag; discuss internally why it\'s stalled (Leo Ho assigned).\n- TRAN-491 (High): Email notifications for customer group changes — also backlog.\n- TRAN-1027: Staging \'True Orders\' issue explicitly Blocked by Nexcess (hosting vendor) — external dependency.\n- TRAN-1071: Klaviyo 6-month campaign calendar is On Hold (Mahmoud) — reason not captured in snapshot; confirm before meeting.\n- Stability/performance cluster: TRAN-641 (recurring 504 timeouts), TRAN-1119 (New Relic response-time spikes), TRAN-1131 (UptimeRobot downtime review) — all backlogged; collectively these represent site reliability risk worth triaging.\n- Two items unassigned: TRAN-697 (Instant Purchase visibility), TRAN-674 (GA banner click tracking), TRAN-868, TRAN-701 — need owners.\n\nITEMS NEEDING CUSTOMER INPUT: [Information Not Available] — no items flagged in the \'needs_customer_input\' category in the Jira snapshot. However, consider raising with Kelly: (1) approval/scheduling of the two ready-for-deployment items, (2) priorities for the marketing backlog (Klaviyo campaign calendar on hold, Rebuild Kit promo email TRAN-821, promo campaign TRAN-935), and (3) backlog prioritization given volume.\n\nKEY TALKING POINTS & RECOMMENDATIONS:\n1. Lead with the AI Chatbot launch as the headline win; frame TRAN-1290 (conversation analysis) as the next optimization step.\n2. Get client sign-off to deploy TRAN-1275 and TRAN-1283.\n3. Internally: escalate the SessionReaper security hotfix (TRAN-1286) — do not let this age.\n4. Address why the Highest-priority TRAN-653 remains in backlog; either re-prioritize or downgrade.\n5. Propose a backlog grooming session — 23 backlog items with several 500/600/700-series (aging) tickets.\n6. Confirm status/reason for the On Hold Klaviyo campaign calendar before the meeting.\n7. Assign owners to the 4 unassigned tickets.','Status Update Before Our Meeting – Transpart','<p>Hi Kelly,</p><p>Ahead of our meeting on Wednesday, July 22, 2026, here\'s a quick summary of where things stand:</p><p><strong>Completed Since Last Meeting</strong></p><ul><li>The AI Chatbot is now live on the production site, and we\'ve started the optimization phase.</li><li>Fixed the issue where \'Login as Customer\' was redirecting to the login page instead of opening the customer\'s session; the fix has been reviewed and deployed.</li><li>Resolved the discrepancy between the out-of-stock flag and how products actually appear on the storefront.</li><li>Completed a full dry run test as part of the chatbot rollout.</li></ul><p><strong>Currently In Progress</strong></p><ul><li>Catalog update to implement bundle and configurable products.</li><li>Analyzing chatbot conversations to improve response quality following the launch.</li><li>Verifying the connections with ShipStation and Klaviyo.</li><li>Investigating and resolving an issue with the product kits import process.</li><li>Applying a recommended platform security update to keep the site protected.</li></ul><p><strong>Ready for Deployment</strong></p><ul><li>Estimated shipping rules and hold-status email notifications — ready to go live; we\'d like to confirm a deployment window with you.</li><li>Simplified purchase flow and display for Rebuild Kits / Packages — also ready for deployment pending your go-ahead.</li></ul><p><strong>Items Where We\'d Value Your Input</strong></p><ul><li>Approval and preferred timing for the two deployments listed above.</li><li>Prioritization of upcoming marketing initiatives, including the email campaign calendar and the Rebuild Kit promotional campaign, so we can schedule them appropriately.</li></ul><p><strong>Proposed Agenda</strong></p><ol><li>Recap of completed work, including the AI Chatbot launch</li><li>Approval and scheduling of the two items ready for deployment</li><li>Update on catalog work (bundle and configurable products)</li><li>Marketing initiatives and campaign priorities</li><li>Backlog review and prioritization for the coming weeks</li></ol><p>Please let us know if you\'d like to add anything to the agenda. Looking forward to speaking with you.</p><p>Best,</p>',NULL,NULL,'\"1. Wins & Completed Work Recap – AI Chatbot production launch, login-as-customer fix, stock display fix (15 min)\\n2. Deployment Approvals – Estimated shipping rules/hold-status notifications and simplified Rebuild Kit purchase flow: confirm client sign-off and deployment window (15 min)\\n3. In-Progress Update – Bundle & configurable products catalog work, chatbot conversation analysis, ShipStation/Klaviyo connection checks, product kits import issue (20 min)\\n4. Marketing Priorities – Klaviyo campaign calendar (currently on hold), Rebuild Kit promo email, and promo campaign scheduling (15 min)\\n5. Backlog Review & Prioritization – Triage high-priority backlog items (UPS order grid coloring, customer group email notifications) and site reliability items (504 timeouts, response-time spikes) (20 min)\\n6. Next Steps, Owners & Wrap-Up (15 min)\"','{\"other\": [{\"key\": \"TRAN-1275\", \"status\": \"Ready for Deployment\", \"summary\": \"Configure Estimated Shipping Rules & Hold Status Email Notifications\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-21T16:32:52.211-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Mostafa Naguib\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}, {\"key\": \"TRAN-1283\", \"status\": \"Ready for Deployment\", \"summary\": \"Simplify Purchase Flow & Display for Rebuild Kits / Packages\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-21T05:13:23.896-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Mostafa Naguib\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}], \"in_progress\": [{\"key\": \"TRAN-268\", \"status\": \"In Progress\", \"summary\": \"Project Management \", \"updated\": \"2026-07-21T16:53:11.190-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Nour eldin ayman\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}, {\"key\": \"TRAN-1292\", \"status\": \"Ready For Dev\", \"summary\": \"Merge eDesk accounts of Nour and JP to use 