OMPLETED SINCE LAST MEETING (1):\n- CMBR2-2192: Add food safe icon to selected SKUs in bulk (Medium, Nour eldin ayman) — Done as of July 27.\n\nIN PROGRESS / READY FOR DEV (10):\n- CMBR2-2188: Product Page - FAQ/Specification Vertical Layout Design Implementation (High, Jean Paul Hanna, Ready For Dev)\n- CMBR2-2187: Main product image does not update when selecting different variant swatches on PDP (High, Donia Khaled, Ready For Dev)\n- CMBR2-2185: Update CTA Buttons on Homepage \'New Products\' Carousel (IT, EN, DE) (High, Jean Paul Hanna, Ready For Dev)\n- CMBR2-2179: Text truncated on \'Confezione\' button under order quantity filter (Low, Donia Khaled, In Progress)\n- CMBR2-934: Project Management (Medium, Nour eldin ayman, In Progress — ongoing PM tracking ticket)\n- CMBR2-2169: Optimize Deployment Process (High, Mostafa Naguib, In Progress)\n- CMBR2-2191: Mass Update Configurable Defaults (Medium, Jean Paul Hanna, Ready For Dev)\n- CMBR2-2190: Create Backend Management Video (Medium, Nour eldin ayman, Ready For Dev)\n- CMBR2-2189: Integrate Trusted Shops Trustbadge on de-at and it-it shops (Medium, Jean Paul Hanna, Ready For Dev)\n- CMBR2-2186: Improve Color Filter Component (Accessibility, Data Check, & Styling) (Medium, Donia Khaled, Ready For Dev)\n\nREADY FOR REVIEW / QA ON STAGING (2 — both Highest priority):\n- CMBR2-2091: Apply Adobe Commerce / Magento Security Patch APSB26-49 (Highest, Nour eldin ayman) — updated this morning; needs Cambro sign-off on staging so we can schedule production deployment ASAP given it\'s a security patch.\n- CMBR2-2174: B2B Customer: Product prices incorrectly display with VAT included (Highest, Nour eldin ayman) — sitting in QA on staging since July 22; needs customer validation to move forward.\n\nBLOCKERS & RISKS:\n- No formal blockers in Jira. However, two Highest-priority items are sitting in QA on staging awaiting validation — the security patch (CMBR2-2091) carries risk if production deployment is delayed. Recommend pushing for a validation/deployment date in the meeting.\n- Six of ten in-progress items are in \'Ready For Dev\' but not yet actively being worked — worth reviewing dev capacity and confirming which High-priority items (2188, 2187, 2185) pick up next.\n\nITEMS NEEDING CUSTOMER INPUT: None formally flagged in Jira. In practice, we need Cambro staging review/approval on CMBR2-2091 and CMBR2-2174.\n\nKEY TALKING POINTS & RECOMMENDATIONS:\n1. Lead with the security patch (CMBR2-2091) — get commitment on staging sign-off and agree a production deployment window.\n2. Get validation on the B2B VAT pricing fix (CMBR2-2174) — high-impact for B2B customers.\n3. Confirm prioritization order for the three High-priority Ready For Dev items (PDP FAQ/spec layout, variant image swatch bug, homepage CTA buttons).\n4. Mention the completed food safe icon bulk update as a quick win.\n5. Briefly note internal deployment process optimization work (CMBR2-2169) — frame as improving release speed and reliability.\n6. Backend Management Video (CMBR2-2190) — confirm scope/expectations with Cambro before dev starts.\n7. Trusted Shops Trustbadge integration (CMBR2-2189) — confirm any account/credential details needed from Cambro side, if applicable.','Status Update Before Our Meeting – Cambro','<p>Hi Cambro team,</p><p>Ahead of our meeting on Wednesday, July 29, 2026, here\'s a quick summary of where things stand:</p><p><strong>Completed Since Last Meeting</strong></p><ul><li>Food safe icon has been added to the selected products in bulk.</li></ul><p><strong>Currently In Progress</strong></p><ul><li>Product page FAQ/specification vertical layout design implementation.</li><li>Fix for the main product image not updating when selecting different variant swatches on the product page.</li><li>Updating the call-to-action buttons on the homepage \"New Products\" carousel (Italian, English, and German).</li><li>Fixing the truncated text on the \"Confezione\" button under the order quantity filter.</li><li>Improvements to the deployment process to make releases faster and more reliable.</li><li>Mass update of configurable product defaults.</li><li>Creation of a backend management video guide.</li><li>Integration of the Trusted Shops Trustbadge on the Austrian and Italian shops.</li><li>Improvements to the color filter component (accessibility, data accuracy, and styling).</li></ul><p><strong>Items Needing Your Input</strong></p><ul><li>Two items are on the staging site awaiting your review and approval (details below). Your sign-off will allow us to schedule them for production — the security update in particular is time-sensitive.</li></ul><p><strong>Items Ready for Review</strong></p><ul><li>The latest Adobe Commerce security patch has been applied and is ready for your review on staging.</li><li>The fix for B2B customer prices incorrectly displaying with VAT included is ready for your review on staging.</li></ul><p><strong>Proposed Agenda</strong></p><ol><li>Review and sign-off plan for the security update and B2B VAT pricing fix currently on staging.</li><li>Walkthrough of completed work and current progress.</li><li>Prioritization of upcoming high-priority items (product page layout, variant image fix, homepage carousel buttons).</li><li>Open discussion and next steps.</li></ol><p>Please let us know if you\'d like to add anything to the agenda. Looking forward to speaking with you.</p><p>Best,</p>',NULL,NULL,'\"1. Security patch & B2B VAT pricing fix – staging review status and production deployment scheduling (15 min)\\n2. Review of completed work and items currently in progress (15 min)\\n3. Prioritization of high-priority upcoming items: PDP FAQ/spec layout, variant swatch image fix, homepage \'New Products\' CTA updates (15 min)\\n4. Scope confirmation for supporting items: backend management video, Trusted Shops Trustbadge integration, configurable defaults mass update (15 min)\\n5. Open discussion, questions, and next steps (15 min)\"','{\"other\": [