 items awaiting customer input.\n\nCOMPLETED SINCE LAST MEETING (5):\n- TRAN-1296 (Critical, Jean Paul Hanna): Products couldn\'t be added to cart despite green success message — resolved. This was our highest-severity item; worth highlighting the quick turnaround.\n- TRAN-1295 (High, Nour eldin ayman): Admin Min/Max Transit Days changes not reflecting on front-end checkout — resolved.\n- TRAN-1294 (Medium, Nour eldin ayman): Incorrect shipping methods displayed for US and International addresses at checkout — resolved.\n- TRAN-1286 (Medium, Mostafa Naguib): Security hotfix applied for CVE-2025-54236 (SessionReaper) on Adobe Commerce 2.4.7-p7 — resolved. Frame to customer as proactive security maintenance; avoid CVE jargon in email.\n- TRAN-1275 (Medium, Mostafa Naguib): Configured Estimated Shipping Rules & Hold Status Email Notifications — resolved.\n\nIN PROGRESS (3):\n- TRAN-1291 (Ready For Dev, Nour eldin ayman): Check connection with ShipStation and Klaviyo — queued for development.\n- TRAN-1290 (In Progress, Nour eldin ayman): Analyze chatbot conversation with AI — actively being worked.\n- TRAN-1283 (REWORK, Mostafa Naguib): Simplify Purchase Flow & Display for Rebuild Kits / Packages — flagged for REWORK. RISK: This is the only item that has bounced back; team should be aligned on the rework reason before the meeting in case the customer asks about timeline. Rework reason: [Information Not Available] — confirm with Mostafa before the call.\n\nBLOCKERS/RISKS:\n- No blocked or on-hold items in the snapshot.\n- TRAN-1283 rework status is the main delivery risk to monitor; confirm revised timeline internally.\n\nITEMS NEEDING CUSTOMER INPUT: None per snapshot. However, consider proactively asking whether the customer wants a demo/validation of the Rebuild Kits purchase flow once rework completes.\n\nITEMS READY FOR REVIEW: None.\n\nKEY TALKING POINTS & RECOMMENDATIONS:\n1. Lead with the strong week: 5 tickets closed including one Critical (add-to-cart failure) and one High (transit days) — both customer-visible checkout issues.\n2. Mention the security hotfix as proactive platform protection (keep it non-technical for the customer).\n3. Set expectations on TRAN-1283 rework — get the rework reason and revised ETA from Mostafa beforehand.\n4. Confirm scope/expectations for the ShipStation and Klaviyo connection check (TRAN-1291) since Klaviyo is part of the client\'s stack.\n5. Ask customer for feedback goals on the AI chatbot conversation analysis (TRAN-1290) — what insights do they want from it?\n6. No customer blockers exist — good opportunity to discuss upcoming priorities and backlog grooming for next sprint.','Status Update Before Our Meeting – Transpart','<p>Hi Kelly,</p><p>Ahead of our meeting on Wednesday, July 29, 2026, here\'s a quick summary of where things stand:</p><p><strong>Completed Since Last Meeting</strong></p><ul><li>Fixed the issue where products could not be added to the cart even though a success message appeared.</li><li>Resolved the issue where admin changes to Min/Max Transit Days were not showing at checkout.</li><li>Corrected the shipping methods displayed for US and International addresses at checkout.</li><li>Applied an important security update to keep the store protected on the latest platform version.</li><li>Configured the Estimated Shipping Rules and Hold Status email notifications.</li></ul><p><strong>Currently In Progress</strong></p><ul><li>Verifying the connections with ShipStation and Klaviyo.</li><li>Analyzing chatbot conversations to gather customer insights.</li><li>Refining the simplified purchase flow and display for Rebuild Kits / Packages.</li></ul><p><strong>Blockers / Items Needing Your Input</strong></p><ul><li>None at this time — nothing is currently waiting on your team.</li></ul><p><strong>Items Ready for Review</strong></p><ul><li>None at this time.</li></ul><p><strong>Proposed Agenda for Our Meeting</strong></p><ol><li>Review of completed items, including the checkout and shipping fixes.</li><li>Update on the Rebuild Kits / Packages purchase flow improvements.</li><li>Status of the ShipStation and Klaviyo connection checks.</li><li>Discussion of the chatbot conversation analysis and desired insights.</li><li>Priorities and planning for the upcoming week.</li></ol><p>Please let us know if you\'d like to add anything to the agenda. Looking forward to speaking with you.</p><p>Best,</p>','Status Update Before Our Meeting – Transpart','<p>Hi Kelly,</p><p>Ahead of our meeting on Wednesday, July 29, 2026, here\'s a quick summary of where things stand:</p><p><strong>Completed Since Last Meeting</strong></p><ul><li>Fixed the issue where products could not be added to the cart even though a success message appeared.</li><li>Resolved the issue where admin changes to Min/Max Transit Days were not showing at checkout.</li><li>Corrected the shipping methods displayed for US and International addresses at checkout.</li><li>Applied an important security update to keep the store protected on the latest platform version.</li><li>Configured the Estimated Shipping Rules and Hold Status email notifications.</li></ul><p><strong>Currently In Progress</strong></p><ul><li>Verifying the connections with ShipStation and Klaviyo.</li><li>Analyzing chatbot conversations to gather customer insights.</li><li>Refining the simplified purchase flow and display for Rebuild Kits / Packages.</li></ul><p><strong>Blockers / Items Needing Your Input</strong></p><ul><li>None at this time — nothing is currently waiting on your team.</li></ul><p><strong>Items Ready for Review</strong></p><ul><li>None at this time.</li></ul><p><strong>Proposed Agenda for Our Meeting</strong></p><ol><li>Review of completed items, including the checkout and shipping fixes.</li><li>Update on the Rebuild Kits / Packages purchase flow improvements.</li><li>Status of the ShipStation and Klaviyo connection checks.</li><li>Discussion of the chatbot conversation analysis and desired insights.</li><li>Priorities and planning for the upcoming week.</li></ol><p>Please let us know if you\'d like to add anything to the agenda. Looking forward to speaking with you.</p><p>Best,</p>','\"1. Wins & completed work review — checkout fixes (add-to-cart, transit days, shipping methods), security update, and shipping/notification configuration (15 min)\\n2. Rebuild Kits / Packages purchase flow — rework status, revised expectations, and customer feedback (20 min)\\n3. ShipStation & Klaviyo connection check — scope confirmation and any credentials/access needed (15 min)\\n4. AI chatbot conversation analysis — progress update and alignment on desired insights/outcomes (15 min)\\n5. Upcoming priorities, backlog review, and next steps (15 min)\"','{\"other\": [], \"in_progress\": [{\"key\": \"TRAN-1291\", \"status\": \"Ready For Dev\", \"summary\": \"Check connection with ShipStation and Klaviyo\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-29T16:19:09.353-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Nour eldin ayman\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}, {\"key\": \"TRAN-1290\", \"status\": \"In Progress\", \"summary\": \"Analyze chatbot conversation with AI\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-29T15:58:40.763-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Nour eldin ayman\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}, {\"key\": \"TRAN-1283\", \"status\": \"REWORK\", \"summary\": \"Simplify Purchase Flow & Display for Rebuild Kits / Packages\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-28T14:40:06.888-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Mostafa Naguib\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}], \"snapshot_at\": \"2026-07-29T20:19:40.443998Z\", \"total_count\": 8, \"high_priority\": [{\"key\": \"TRAN-1295\", \"status\": \"Done\", \"summary\": \"Admin Min/Max Transit Days changes not reflecting on front-end checkout\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-27T16:50:09.855-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Nour eldin ayman\", \"priority\": \"High\"}], \"ready_for_review\": [], \"recently_updated\": [{\"key\": \"TRAN-1291\", \"status\": \"Ready For Dev\", \"summary\": \"Check connection with ShipStation and Klaviyo\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-29T16: