Text truncated on the \\\"Confezione\\\" button under order quantity filter.\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-31T18:07:19.470-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Mostafa Naguib\", \"priority\": \"Low\"}, {\"key\": \"CMBR2-2187\", \"status\": \"Ready for Deployment\", \"summary\": \"Main product image does not update when selecting different variant swatches on PDP\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-31T10:50:29.477-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Mostafa Naguib\", \"priority\": \"Highest\"}, {\"key\": \"CMBR2-2170\", \"status\": \"In Progress\", \"summary\": \"Export Active Products for \'de-de\' and \'it-it\' Stores for Bulk Title Update\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-31T08:09:09.761-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Nour eldin ayman\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}, {\"key\": \"CMBR2-2123\", \"status\": \"Ready For Dev\", \"summary\": \"Inconsistent font rendering in mini-cart across different locales (en-de vs en-at)\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-30T23:38:28.712-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Donia Khaled\", \"priority\": \"Lowest\"}, {\"key\": \"CMBR2-2192\", \"status\": \"Done\", \"summary\": \"Add food safe icon to selected SKUs in bulk\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-29T13:25:52.389-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Nour eldin ayman\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}], \"blocked_or_on_hold\": [], \"needs_customer_input\": [], \"completed_since_last_meeting\": [{\"key\": \"CMBR2-2167\", \"status\": \"Done\", \"summary\": \"Corrupted UI PDP Header in en-it\", \"updated\": \"2026-08-05T06:10:15.064-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Donia Khaled\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}, {\"key\": \"CMBR2-2192\", \"status\": \"Done\", \"summary\": \"Add food safe icon to selected SKUs in bulk\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-29T13:25:52.389-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Nour eldin ayman\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}]}',NULL,'2026-08-05 15:45:22','cdikmen@cambro.com','[\"bcourcelle@cambro.com\", \"spaxia@cambro.com\", \"iaydin@cambro.com\", \"jp@technopath.co\", \"donia@technopath.co\"]',NULL,NULL,'openrouter','~anthropic/claude-fable-latest',NULL,'2026-08-05 15:43:50',NULL,NULL,'2026-08-05 15:43:50','2026-08-05 15:45:22'),(9,247,'TRAN','project = TRAN AND updated >= \'2026-07-29\' ORDER BY updated DESC','PROJECT HEALTH: Overall status is moderate/stable. Work is progressing across 6 tracked items, but there is one item in REWORK and one investigation sitting in the backlog that touches pricing accuracy at checkout — a customer-experience risk that should be prioritized.\n\nCOMPLETED SINCE LAST MEETING:\n- TRAN-1297: Cancel Nexcess subscription for staging (Done, Nour eldin ayman, updated 2026-07-31). Cost-saving housekeeping item — worth mentioning briefly as a positive.\n\nIN PROGRESS:\n- TRAN-1283: Simplify Purchase Flow & Display for Rebuild Kits / Packages (REWORK, Jean Paul Hanna, updated 2026-08-05). NOTE: This is in REWORK status — team should be prepared to explain internally why rework was needed and confirm revised timeline before the meeting. Do not surface \'rework\' framing to the client; position as refinement in progress.\n- TRAN-1301: Update Website to Use ShipStation UPS International Rates (Ready For Dev, Donia Khaled, HIGH priority, updated 2026-08-05). Highest priority item — confirm dev start date and estimated delivery so we can give the client a concrete timeline.\n- TRAN-1290: Analyze chatbot conversation with AI (In Progress, Nour eldin ayman, updated 2026-08-04).\n- TRAN-1291: Check connection with ShipStation and Klaviyo (In Progress, Nour eldin ayman, updated 2026-08-03).\n\nBLOCKED / ON HOLD:\n- TRAN-1300: Investigate pricing hierarchy + checkout price discrepancy (ref SUP-9281) (BACKLOG, Donia Khaled, updated 2026-08-05). RISK: Checkout price discrepancies can directly impact revenue and customer trust. Recommend discussing prioritization internally before the meeting — client may raise this, especially given the linked support ticket SUP-9281. Blocking reason: [Information Not Available] — confirm with Donia before the meeting.\n\nNEEDS CUSTOMER INPUT: No items are currently flagged as needing customer input in the Jira snapshot. However, consider whether the client should confirm expected behavior for the pricing hierarchy investigation (TRAN-1300) and validate requirements for UPS International rates (TRAN-1301).\n\nITEMS READY FOR REVIEW: None.\n\nKEY TALKING POINTS & RECOMMENDATIONS:\n1. Lead with the high-priority ShipStation UPS International Rates work — confirm scope and timeline with Donia beforehand.\n2. Be ready to explain the rebuild kits purchase flow status (TRAN-1283 in REWORK) — align internally on what changed and the revised ETA.\n3. Proactively address the checkout price discrepancy investigation (TRAN-1300) — the client may already be aware via the referenced support ticket. Recommend proposing to move it out of backlog.\n4. Provide brief updates on chatbot AI analysis and ShipStation/Klaviyo connection checks — confirm with Nour whether any findings are ready to share.\n5. Confirm staging subscription cancellation is complete with no side effects on the client\'s environments.','Status Update Before Our Meeting – Transpart','<p>Hi Kelly,</p><p>Ahead of our meeting on Wednesday, August 5, 2026, here\'s a quick summary of where things stand:</p><p><strong>Completed Since Last Meeting</strong></p><ul><li>Cancelled the staging environment hosting subscription that was no longer needed, reducing unnecessary costs.</li></ul><p><strong>Currently In Progress</strong></p><ul><li>Simplifying the purchase flow and display for Rebuild Kits and Packages to make ordering easier for your customers.</li><li>Updating the website to use ShipStation UPS International shipping rates (high priority) — this is queued for development.</li><li>Analyzing chatbot conversations with AI to surface insights from customer interactions.</li><li>Verifying the connections between your store, ShipStation, and Klaviyo to ensure everything is syncing correctly.</li></ul><p><strong>Blockers / Items Needing Your Input</strong></p><ul><li>We have an investigation queued regarding a pricing display difference some customers may see at checkout. We\'d like to discuss prioritization with you and confirm the expected pricing behavior on your end.</li></ul><p><strong>Items Ready for Review</strong></p><ul><li>None at this time.</li></ul><p><strong>Proposed Agenda</strong></p><ol><li>International shipping rates update — scope and timeline</li><li>Rebuild Kits / Packages purchase flow — progress update</li><li>Checkout pricing investigation — prioritization and expected behavior</li><li>Chatbot analysis and ShipStation/Klaviyo connection updates</li><li>Upcoming priorities and next steps</li></ol><p>Please let us know if you\'d like to add anything to the agenda. Looking forward to speaking with you.</p><p>Best,</p>','Status Update Before Our Meeting – Transpart','<p>Hi Kelly,</p><p>Ahead of our meeting on Wednesday, August 5, 2026, here\'s a quick summary of where things stand:</p><p><strong>Completed Since Last Meeting</strong></p><ul><li>Cancelled the staging environment hosting subscription that was no longer needed, reducing unnecessary costs.</li></ul><p><strong>Currently In Progress</strong></p><ul><li>Simplifying the purchase flow and display for Rebuild Kits and Packages to make ordering easier for your customers.</li><li>Updating the website to use ShipStation UPS International shipping rates (high priority) — this is queued for development.</li><li>Analyzing chatbot conversations with AI to surface insights from customer interactions.</li><li>Verifying the connections between your store, ShipStation, and Klaviyo to ensure everything is syncing correctly.</li></ul><p><strong>Blockers / Items Needing Your Input</strong></p><ul><li>We have an investigation queued regarding a pricing display difference some customers may see at checkout. We\'d like to discuss prioritization with you and confirm the expected pricing behavior on your end.</li></ul><p><strong>Items Ready for Review</strong></p><ul><li>None at this time.</li></ul><p><strong>Proposed Agenda</strong></p><ol><li>International shipping rates update — scope and timeline</li><li>Rebuild Kits / Packages purchase flow — progress update</li><li>Checkout pricing investigation — prioritization and expected behavior</li><li>Chatbot analysis and ShipStation/Klaviyo connection updates</li><li>Upcoming priorities and next steps</li></ol><p>Please let us know if you\'d like to add anything to the agenda. Looking forward to speaking with you.</p><p>Best,</p>','\"1. Welcome & recap of completed work, including staging subscription cleanup (5 min)\\n2. ShipStation UPS International Rates update — scope confirmation and delivery timeline (10 min)\\n3. Rebuild Kits / Packages purchase flow — current progress and next steps (10 min)\\n4. Checkout pricing discrepancy investigation — prioritization discussion and confirming expected pricing behavior (10 min)\\n5. Updates on chatbot AI conversation analysis and ShipStation/Klaviyo connection verification (10 min)\\n6. Open items, client questions, and priorities for next week (10 min)\"','{\"other\": [], \"in_progress\": [{\"key\": \"TRAN-1283\", \"status\": \"REWORK\", \"summary\": \"Simplify Purchase Flow & Display for Rebuild Kits / Packages\", \"updated\": \"2026-08-05T15:24:04.523-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Jean Paul Hanna\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}, {\"key\": \"TRAN-1301\", \"status\": \"Ready For Dev\", \"summary\": \"Update Website to Use ShipStation UPS International Rates\", \"updated\": \"2026-08-05T15:19:50.533-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Donia Khaled\", \"priority\": \"High\"}, {\"key\": \"TRAN-1290\", \"status\": \"In Progress\", \"summary\": \"Analyze chatbot conversation with AI\", \"updated\": \"2026-08-04T10:28:45.806-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Nour eldin ayman\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}, {\"key\": \"TRAN-1291\", \"status\": \"In Progress\", \"summary\": \"Check connection with ShipStation and Klaviyo\", \"updated\": \"2026-08-03T13:14:10.404-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Nour eldin ayman\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}], \"